meta {
  name: 40-vault-ciphers
  seq: 40
}

docs {
  Items of a personal vault: create, read, change, move, archive, trash,
  restore, delete, import, attachments.

  Most of these calls are made by the Rust SDK, not by TypeScript, so the
  coverage report (built from TypeScript calls) missed them. Their list comes
  from the SDK source; see `plans/261109-2031-official-vault-endpoints/plan.md`.

  The SDK reads every cipher answer with `TryFrom<CipherResponseModel>`
  (`crates/bitwarden-vault/src/cipher/cipher.rs`): `type`, `creationDate` and
  `revisionDate` are required, the rest is optional.
}
